::SQL UNIQUE::
What is true about the Unique and Primary keys?
{
    =Unique can have one or more NULL values but Primary Keys cannot.
    ~Unique can have no NULL values but Primary can have NULL values.
    ~Both can have duplicate values.
    ~None of the above.
}

::SQL UNIQUE::
What is the primary purpose of a unique key constraint in a database table?
{
    ~To enforce referential integrity between two tables.
    ~To specify the default value for a column.
    =To ensure that the values in a column are unique within the table.
    ~To prevent NULL values from being inserted into a column.
}